Adapted copies (changed by this project; changes listed)
---------------------------------------------------------
- scripts/uri-guard.mjs, from examples/agent-hook-plugin/scripts/uri-guard.mjs:
  reads the client id from argv[3] (the Kiro hook command is
  `uri-guard.mjs pre-tool-use kiro`) and defaults to "kiro".
- hosts/index.mjs, from examples/agent-hook-plugin/hosts/index.mjs: registers
  only the Kiro host.
- hosts/kiro-capture.mjs, from examples/agent-hook-plugin/hosts/zcode-capture.mjs:
  the same file with "Zcode" renamed to "Kiro".
- plugin.json and hosts/kiro/openviking.integration.json, from the upstream files
  of the same schema: own name, description, author, license, client and version.
- kiro-assets/skills/openviking-memory/SKILL.md, from
  examples/skills/openviking-memory/SKILL.md: Kiro wording and tool names.

Files written for this project that follow an upstream pattern
---------------------------------------------------------------
- hosts/kiro.mjs follows the structure of the upstream ZCode adapter
  (hosts/zcode.mjs) and Kimi Code adapter (hosts/kimicode.mjs).
- hosts/kiro-turns.mjs and hosts/kiro-session.mjs follow the idea of
  hosts/kimicode-turns.mjs (decode the host's own transcript into turns).
- hosts/kiro-guard.mjs wraps the shared evaluateUriGuard in an "ask" envelope.
- hosts/kiro/.mcp.json is a reference template shaped like hosts/zcode/.mcp.json.
- scripts/install.mjs and scripts/uninstall.mjs mirror the behavior of
  examples/memory-plugin-shared/install.sh in Node.
- kiro-assets/steering/openviking-memory.md is original text with the same
  purpose as hosts/cursor/rules/openviking-memory.mdc.

Run-time dependency
-------------------
At run time this package imports the OpenViking shared runtime
(memory-plugin-shared/lib) from the user's own OpenViking installation under
~/.openviking/agent-integrations/. That runtime is not included in this
repository.

The Kiro-specific parts (the installer and uninstaller, the Kiro assets, the
upstream-sync tooling and the tests) were written for this project.

